.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt PURGE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm purge
.Nd empty the disk cache
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes out the data waiting to be written, then empties the disk cache:
the file data the system keeps in memory for every mounted volume.
It is for seeing how a program behaves when nothing is cached, as after
a restart.
Only the super-user may run it.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vm_stat 1 ,
.Xr sync 2
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
